Feature: Comprehensive API Security Testing # features/api_security.feature:1
  As a QA engineer
  I want to test various API security scenarios
  So that I can ensure comprehensive security coverage
  @smoke @authentication
  Scenario: Valid token should validate successfully  # features/api_security.feature:10
    Given I have a valid token                        # features/steps/auth_steps.py:27
    When I send a request to "/api/users/me"          # features/steps/auth_steps.py:74
    Then the response should validate token           # features/steps/auth_steps.py:130

  @smoke @authentication
  Scenario: Admin token should validate successfully  # features/api_security.feature:16
    Given I have an admin token                       # features/steps/auth_steps.py:27
    When I send a request to "/api/users/me"          # features/steps/auth_steps.py:74
    Then the response should validate token           # features/steps/auth_steps.py:130

  @smoke @authentication
  Scenario: User token should validate successfully  # features/api_security.feature:22
    Given I have a user token                        # features/steps/auth_steps.py:27
    When I send a request to "/api/users/me"         # features/steps/auth_steps.py:74
    Then the response should validate token          # features/steps/auth_steps.py:130

  @smoke @authentication
  Scenario: Invalid token should return 401  # features/api_security.feature:28
    Given I have an invalid token            # features/steps/auth_steps.py:27
    When I send a request to "/api/users/me" # features/steps/auth_steps.py:74
    Then the response should expect 401      # features/steps/auth_steps.py:130

  @smoke @authentication
  Scenario: Missing token should return 401  # features/api_security.feature:34
    Given I have no token                    # features/steps/auth_steps.py:27
    When I send a request to "/api/users/me" # features/steps/auth_steps.py:74
    Then the response should expect 401      # features/steps/auth_steps.py:130

  @authorization @role-based
  Scenario: Admin token should allow access to admin endpoint  # features/api_security.feature:40
    Given I have an admin token                                # features/steps/auth_steps.py:27
    When I send a request to "/api/admin/users"                # features/steps/auth_steps.py:74
    Then the response should access allowed                    # features/steps/auth_steps.py:130

  @authorization @role-based
  Scenario: User token should be denied access to admin endpoint  # features/api_security.feature:46
    Given I have a user token                                     # features/steps/auth_steps.py:27
    When I send a request to "/api/admin/users"                   # features/steps/auth_steps.py:74
    Then the response should access denied                        # features/steps/auth_steps.py:130

  @authorization @role-based
  Scenario: Valid token (admin) should allow access to admin endpoint  # features/api_security.feature:52
    Given I have a valid token                                         # features/steps/auth_steps.py:27
    When I send a request to "/api/admin/users"                        # features/steps/auth_steps.py:74
    Then the response should access allowed                            # features/steps/auth_steps.py:130

  @authorization @role-based
  Scenario: Invalid token should return 401 on admin endpoint  # features/api_security.feature:58
    Given I have an invalid token                              # features/steps/auth_steps.py:27
    When I send a request to "/api/admin/users"                # features/steps/auth_steps.py:74
    Then the response should expect 401                        # features/steps/auth_steps.py:130

  @authorization @role-based
  Scenario: Missing token should return 401 on admin endpoint  # features/api_security.feature:64
    Given I have no token                                      # features/steps/auth_steps.py:27
    When I send a request to "/api/admin/users"                # features/steps/auth_steps.py:74
    Then the response should expect 401                        # features/steps/auth_steps.py:130

  @security @edge-cases
  Scenario: Health check endpoint should be accessible without authentication  # features/api_security.feature:70
    Given I have no token                                                      # features/steps/auth_steps.py:27
    When I send a request to "/api/health"                                     # features/steps/auth_steps.py:74
    Then the response should access allowed                                    # features/steps/auth_steps.py:130

  @security @negative
  Scenario: Invalid token format should be rejected  # features/api_security.feature:76
    Given I have an invalid token                    # features/steps/auth_steps.py:27
    When I send a request to "/api/admin/users"      # features/steps/auth_steps.py:74
    Then the response should expect 401              # features/steps/auth_steps.py:130

  @security @negative
  Scenario: Missing token on protected endpoint should return 401  # features/api_security.feature:82
    Given I have no token                                          # features/steps/auth_steps.py:27
    When I send a request to "/api/admin/users"                    # features/steps/auth_steps.py:74
    Then the response should expect 401                            # features/steps/auth_steps.py:130

Feature: API Authentication and Authorization # features/auth.feature:1
  As a developer
  I want to validate API security
  So that I can ensure my API endpoints are properly protected
  Scenario: Valid token should grant access to user profile  # features/auth.feature:6
    Given I have a valid token                               # features/steps/auth_steps.py:27
    When I send a request to "/api/users/me"                 # features/steps/auth_steps.py:74
    Then the response should validate token                  # features/steps/auth_steps.py:130

  Scenario: Invalid token should return 401  # features/auth.feature:11
    Given I have an invalid token            # features/steps/auth_steps.py:27
    When I send a request to "/api/users/me" # features/steps/auth_steps.py:74
    Then the response should expect 401      # features/steps/auth_steps.py:130

  Scenario: Missing token should return 401  # features/auth.feature:16
    Given I have no token                    # features/steps/auth_steps.py:27
    When I send a request to "/api/users/me" # features/steps/auth_steps.py:74
    Then the response should expect 401      # features/steps/auth_steps.py:130

  Scenario: User token should be denied access to admin endpoint  # features/auth.feature:21
    Given I have a user token                                     # features/steps/auth_steps.py:27
    When I send a request to "/api/admin/users"                   # features/steps/auth_steps.py:74
    Then the response should access denied                        # features/steps/auth_steps.py:130

  Scenario: Admin token should allow access to admin endpoint  # features/auth.feature:26
    Given I have an admin token                                # features/steps/auth_steps.py:27
    When I send a request to "/api/admin/users"                # features/steps/auth_steps.py:74
    Then the response should access allowed                    # features/steps/auth_steps.py:130

Feature: Edge Cases and Boundary Conditions # features/edge_cases.feature:1
  As a security tester
  I want to test edge cases and boundary conditions
  So that I can ensure the API handles unexpected scenarios correctly
  Scenario: User with valid token accessing non-existent endpoint behavior  # features/edge_cases.feature:6
    Given I have a valid token                                              # features/steps/auth_steps.py:27
    When I send a request to "/api/users/me"                                # features/steps/auth_steps.py:74
    Then the response should validate token                                 # features/steps/auth_steps.py:130

  Scenario: Multiple consecutive invalid token attempts  # features/edge_cases.feature:13
    Given I have an invalid token                        # features/steps/auth_steps.py:27
    When I send a request to "/api/users/me"             # features/steps/auth_steps.py:74
    Then the response should expect 401                  # features/steps/auth_steps.py:130

  Scenario: User token attempting to access admin endpoint multiple times  # features/edge_cases.feature:19
    Given I have a user token                                              # features/steps/auth_steps.py:27
    When I send a request to "/api/admin/users"                            # features/steps/auth_steps.py:74
    Then the response should access denied                                 # features/steps/auth_steps.py:130

  Scenario: Admin token accessing user endpoint  # features/edge_cases.feature:25
    Given I have an admin token                  # features/steps/auth_steps.py:27
    When I send a request to "/api/users/me"     # features/steps/auth_steps.py:74
    Then the response should validate token      # features/steps/auth_steps.py:130

  Scenario: Valid token accessing health check  # features/edge_cases.feature:31
    Given I have a valid token                  # features/steps/auth_steps.py:27
    When I send a request to "/api/health"      # features/steps/auth_steps.py:74
    Then the response should access allowed     # features/steps/auth_steps.py:130

Feature: Complete Authentication Workflow # features/workflow.feature:1
  As a developer
  I want to test complete authentication workflows
  So that I can validate end-to-end security flows
  Scenario: Complete user authentication flow - success path  # features/workflow.feature:6
    Given I have a valid token                                # features/steps/auth_steps.py:27
    When I send a request to "/api/users/me"                  # features/steps/auth_steps.py:74
    Then the response should validate token                   # features/steps/auth_steps.py:130

  Scenario: Complete user authentication flow - unauthorized access attempt  # features/workflow.feature:12
    Given I have an invalid token                                            # features/steps/auth_steps.py:27
    When I send a request to "/api/users/me"                                 # features/steps/auth_steps.py:74
    Then the response should expect 401                                      # features/steps/auth_steps.py:130

  Scenario: Complete admin workflow - authorized admin access  # features/workflow.feature:18
    Given I have an admin token                                # features/steps/auth_steps.py:27
    When I send a request to "/api/admin/users"                # features/steps/auth_steps.py:74
    Then the response should access allowed                    # features/steps/auth_steps.py:130

  Scenario: Complete admin workflow - unauthorized user access  # features/workflow.feature:24
    Given I have a user token                                   # features/steps/auth_steps.py:27
    When I send a request to "/api/admin/users"                 # features/steps/auth_steps.py:74
    Then the response should access denied                      # features/steps/auth_steps.py:130

  Scenario: Complete workflow - missing authentication  # features/workflow.feature:30
    Given I have no token                               # features/steps/auth_steps.py:27
    When I send a request to "/api/users/me"            # features/steps/auth_steps.py:74
    Then the response should expect 401                 # features/steps/auth_steps.py:130

